From: CMI-Mem Contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Register TrajectoryRewardManager in verl reward manager registry

Adds auto-import of TrajectoryRewardManager from training.agentic.reward_manager
so that the "trajectory" reward manager name is recognized by verl's registry.
This is required for Agentic RL training with per-turn dense CMI rewards.

The import is wrapped in try/except so that users who only use batch mode
(without the agentic module) will not see import errors.

--- a/verl/workers/reward_manager/__init__.py
+++ b/verl/workers/reward_manager/__init__.py
@@ -18,6 +18,12 @@ from .dapo import DAPORewardManager
 from .naive import NaiveRewardManager
 from .prime import PrimeRewardManager
 
+# Agentic RL trajectory reward manager (registers "trajectory" in the registry)
+try:
+    from training.agentic.reward_manager import TrajectoryRewardManager  # noqa: F401
+except ImportError:
+    TrajectoryRewardManager = None  # agentic module not available
+
 # Note(haibin.lin): no need to include all reward managers here in case of complicated dependencies
 __all__ = [
     "BatchRewardManager",
